      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BLUE SPARX (1) finished 1.4L off the winner last time out at Belmont after jumping the race favourite. The winkers go on now for the first time and a better barrier today should see him a little closer in the run. Ticks enough boxes to suggests he can score a maiden win third-up. FORCE FIELD (2) disappointed two back but returned to form last start when sitting closer and just missing over 1200m at Belmont, finishing 0.7L off the winner. Parnham sticks and a better barrier this time is a huge boost for his chances. He looks to get every chance in the run. RAW UMBER (3) gets Pike on board today following a fair debut at Belmont when jumping in the market. He'll be better for that effort though and a better showing is on the cards. EYE OF THE SUN (5) caused an upset when beating a lot of these last time out and did so when running good splits. Wouldn't surprise to see her do it again. DUMPLING (8) was sound on resumption and can improve with that run under his belt.",
